e code what needs testing: running with no args or flags should print the version and return 0, unknown arguments should print usage to stderr and return 2, and the version should default to \"dev\" when not set via build flags. Let me draft this as a test task, though I need to verify it fits within the release scope constraints. I'm identifying the specific requirements from prd011-magefiles that the test needs to cover—R1.1, R1.2, R1.4, and R1.5—and determining the correct test file structure. Based on the architecture pattern where test files follow the naming convention of their source, version_test.go is the right approach for testing the cmd/version package. with version_test.go since that matches the architecture document's pattern.\n\nLet me draft the task:\n\nTitle: \"prd011-magefiles R1.1, R1.2, R1.4, R1.5 -- cmd/version unit tests\"\n\nRequirements based on what's in the source code:\n- R1.1: version with no args prints version string to stdout, exits 0\n- R1.2: version defaults to \"dev\" when ldflags not set\n- R1.4: --version and -v flags print version, exit 0\n- R1.5: unknown args print usage to stderr, exit 2\n\nThat's 4 requirements which fits the constraint of \"at most 4 requirements.\"\n\nFor the task title, I need to anchor it to specific PRD requirement IDs. The format should be prd011-magefiles R1.1, R1.2, R1.4, R1.5 -- cmd/version unit tests.\n\nNow for design decisions, I should derive these from the PRD rather than inventing them. Since I don't have the full PRD text, I'll be conservative and reference what I can see in the code. The stitch agent will need to read cmd/version/main.go to understand the implementation. The test file should test the run function directly, which is already separated from main for testability. The exit codes are 0 for success and 2 for usage errors, which the tests need to verify. Writing task requirements... I need to reconsider the approach here—the `run` function is unexported, but since the test file will be in the same `package main`, I can still access it. That works fine. Now I'm thinking through the output redirection strategy for capturing stdout and stderr in the tests. I'm reconsidering whether this is actually the right task to propose, given the constraints around design decisions and scope.\n\nLooking at the remaining work across all rel00.0 use cases, the format, sys, and testutils packages are already complete with full test coverage. The only gap is cmd/version, which needs tests—so this task is correctly scoped and necessary.\n\nFor the title, I should anchor it to the specific PRD requirements as instructed. The task is: \"prd011-magefiles R1.1, R1.2, R1.4, R1.5 -- cmd/version unit tests\"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":45545,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":45545},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c541a6a-1133-4d1e-89d5-5e49df58d45d","uuid":"12e049fc-8ba8-4bdd-a371-646fe484eed6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UzaDQB2t7D72mp68fPS1kd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications accessible to implementers. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds per-utility Go binaries, `pkg/sys/` wraps platform syscalls, `pkg/format/` provides shared formatting, `pkg/testutils/` is the differential testing harness, and `magefiles/` exposes build targets.\n\n**Current Implementation**: All `pkg/` packages exist with code and tests: `pkg/format/` (color, column, size), `pkg/sys/` (fileinfo, terminal), `pkg/testutils/` (difftest). `cmd/version/main.go` exists but has no test file. The code_status analysis shows all rel00.0 use cases as \"not started\", but the source code contradicts this — trusting source code per constraints.\n\n**Current Release**: rel00.0 (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure). Four use cases: uc001-magefiles, uc002-format, uc003-sys, uc004-testutils. The `pkg/` packages (uc002, uc003, uc004) are complete with tests. `cmd/version` (the only generation target of uc001-magefiles per DD7) has implementation but no tests.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nThe only remaining gap in rel00.0 is `cmd/version/version_test.go`. All three `pkg/` packages have both implementation and test files. `cmd/version/main.go` implements prd011-magefiles R1.1, R1.2, R1.4, R1.5 but has no corresponding test file, violating the architecture's convention that each `cmd/` package contains `<utility>_test.go`.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd011-magefiles R1.1, R1.2, R1.4, R1.5 -- cmd/version unit tests\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd011-magefiles.yaml (requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.4, R1.5)\n      - cmd/version/main.go (implementation under test)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/version/version_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Unit tests for the version command covering all four R1.x requirements\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test prd011-magefiles R1.1: running with no arguments prints the version string to stdout and returns exit code 0\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test prd011-magefiles R1.2: when the linker variable is not set, the version string defaults to \\\"dev\\\"\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test prd011-magefiles R1.4: --version and -v flags each print the version string to stdout and return exit code 0\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Test prd011-magefiles R1.5: unrecognized arguments print \\\"usage: version [--version | -v]\\\" to stderr and return exit code 2\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Test the unexported run(args []string) int function directly. It returns the exit code and writes to fmt stdout/stderr, separating exit logic from output logic. The test file uses package main so it can access unexported symbols.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Capture stdout by temporarily replacing os.Stdout with an os.Pipe, matching the pattern used in pkg/sys/terminal_test.go. Same approach for stderr verification.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/version/version_test.go exists, compiles, and uses package main\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/version/ passes with all tests green\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Tests cover all four requirement scenarios: no-args default, dev default value, both flag variants (--version, -v), and unrecognized argument error\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Each test asserts both the return code from run() and the content written to stdout or stderr\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":45545,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":45545},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c541a6a-1133-4d1e-89d5-5e49df58d45d","uuid":"13deff5b-b552-4507-b7e8-590ef1ebd59f"}
